{"type":"text","timestamp":1794540471635,"sessionID":"ses_e2d114b51ffeDlZ2G0EwOc9mR4","part":{"id":"prt_1d2f278b8002E4XvTabvOFF4kq","sessionID":"ses_e2d114b51ffeDlZ2G0EwOc9mR4","messageID":"msg_1d2f263dd001pG8zh1M4IrKkjV","type":"text","text":"T014 complete. The new test file exists and its verify command passes.\n\n**File written**\n`.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-head-length.vitest.ts`\n\nIt renders one head for each of the 63 `TRACKED_COMMANDS` keys through its owner and one for each of the 56 `COMMAND_ROWS` ids through the generated row. Each head is split at `DIRECTIVES_LABEL` and checked against `HEAD_BYTE_LIMIT` (`80 * 4`), checked for a trailing `...` and checked for `<command> (<policy>)`. A synthetic 330-character command case confirms the same check rejects a truncated head. The cases pass `{ childSession: false }` because this worker environment sets `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1`, which otherwise renders start and ask policies as `parent-named only` and would break the policy assertion in every run here.\n\n**Verify output**\n\n```\n RUN  v4.1.12 .../.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime\n\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  120 passed (120)\n   Duration  260ms\n```\n\nCommand: `npx vitest run tests/command-head-length.vitest.ts` run in `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime`. 0 failed, 120 passed, which clears the 45-test floor.\n\n`git status` shows only the new untracked test file. `tasks.md` was not ticked and nothing was committed.\n\nNothing is blocked on you.","time":{"start":1794540468408,"end":1794540471635}}}
